    42	**Engine scope.** Engine v2 covers scheduled-duty models: a finite
    43	validator set; labels with a fixed act time and seat count; committees
    44	or the full validator set, with public assignment conditions;
    45	identity-free honest code (no private key or private randomness); one
    46	global time; a static honest set; finite runs; emission only on ticks.
    47	
    48	Out of scope by decision (user, 2026-09-28): private VRF
    49	self-selection. Also outside v2, each needing a new engine version with a
    50	lift simulation: clock drift (one logical duty at different local
    51	times); signed replies on receipt; explicit compromise or key erasure;
    52	unbounded liveness.
    53	
    54	Additions inside the scope (not covered by existing certificates):
    55	integer stake weights (seat multiplicity, weighted links and quorum
    56	lemmas; the unit-weight FG proofs do not transfer by themselves); fixed
