   205	
   206	Protocol parameters and facets are bound once. Claim constants are NOT
   207	in the instance; they belong to certificates (§5). So one instance can
   208	hold several certified tradeoff points of one claim (for example SA's P1
   209	with (A, Π) and fast P1 with (A_f, Π); SA-PC recovery at h > a and at
   210	a ≤ f with different ρ).
   211	
   212	Facets: `ChainOutputs`, `Proposals` (labels, times, proposal identifier,
   213	`block`, `opening`), `Protected`, `Base`, `Durable`, and the FG facets
   214	of §7. Every output getter reads only `base`. Claims are schemas over
   215	output names. Phase 0 selects an extensible representation for
   216	`FacetBundle`, `FacetNeeds`, `ProtocolParams` and constant records
   217	(typed maps or separate facet records), because adding a field to a
   218	frozen Lean structure changes its declaration.
