   259	The **v1 → v2 simulation is feasible**. The disjoint label sum and per-label seat counts give the correct authentication encoding:
   260	
   261	- Old committee authentication maps to the old-label summand.
   262	- `proposer s` maps to seat 0 of the singleton proposal label for s.
   263	- `proposerOf s` is exactly the holder of that seat.
   264	- Recovering old committee assignments requires the proved bijection, including the dependent `Fin` casts.
   265	- With recording disabled, all duty and proposal payloads use the same post-clock state. Concatenating old duties and proposal duties in the old order preserves emissions.
   266	- `NoRestart` permits the ordinary event-fold simulation. The wrappers must also transport carried authentication, hook predicates, root scope, proposal identifiers and regimes.
   267	
   268	In particular, claims that quantify over `proposerOf` can transfer through the holder equivalence. A forward embedding alone is insufficient for universal claims: every v2 run in the lifted legacy regime needs a corresponding v1 run. Arbitrary v2 assignments outside that regime are not covered. The design now largely states the required work. [Lift proposal](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:211), [old emissions and holders](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainModel/Generic/Run.lean:141), [proposal predicate](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainStatements/Generic/Properties.lean:58).
