   343	
   344	Parameters absent from a row do not affect that field. This table does not authorize changing a protocol parameter with the same name: changing the protocol's η can change P itself.
   345	
   346	The logical premise/conclusion directions are straightforward. To transport a certificate from p to p′, prove that the new regime implies the old regime and that the old conclusion implies the new conclusion. Inhabitation does not follow from either implication. v5's direction list is correct for the listed scalar changes; its schema still needs those actual transport proofs.
   347	
   348	The current regimes have the following prefix behaviour.
   349	
   350	```text
   351	┌───────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   352	│ Regime        │ Prefix-closure status                                               │
   353	├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
   354	│ Sleepy        │ Closed under complete time truncation to a nonnegative horizon.    │
   355	│ StableSleepy  │ Same; preserve E and the awake history used by η.                  │
   356	│ Fast          │ Same; full participation restricts to the shorter interval.        │
   357	│ Outage        │ Not under arbitrary cuts. A cut must be at least b₁.               │
   358	│ FastOutage    │ Same minimum horizon b₁.                                           │
   359	│ Recovery      │ Not under arbitrary cuts. A cut must be at least GST+ρ.            │
   360	│ StrongArmed   │ Not under arbitrary cuts. A cut must be at least b₀.               │
   361	└───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   362	```
   363	
   364	These facts concern complete time prefixes, with assignments unchanged. An event-list prefix halfway through equal-time events can fail `tick_total`. Causal induction therefore needs an execution-prefix interface distinct from the complete-run regimes. The inequality `q_s<d_s` is useful, but the AP theorem must also be usable before `d_s`; it cannot require an assumption about the whole future interval. [Schedule totality](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainStatements/Generic/Conditions.lean:38), [regimes](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainStatements/Generic/Regimes.lean:14), [StrongArmed](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainStatements/Strong/Regimes.lean:19).
   365	
   366	The FG facts **D, E and F have sound proof routes**, with qualifications. D needs the actual inclusive causal cut and the source-to-local-frontier bound. E needs the selected NJ prefix or the named finalized checkpoint and its crossing facts, not an arbitrary height with the right number. F correctly requires a source for both targets and timeouts; an empty height source can coexist with a nonempty finality pair. The source bodies must then be retained from their first transfer, as separate history data. These are consistent with DC and r146. They do not establish v5's universal `HeightRetains`. [Causal construction](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/fgsa-adjudicate.md:563), [two-arm source history](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/fgsa-adjudicate.md:394), [exact client](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/fgsa-fast.md:268).
   367	
   368	The Lean mechanisms are feasible, with the following limits.
   369	
   370	- **Freeze check:** `ConstantInfo.getUsedConstantsAsSet` exists in the pinned toolchain. It inspects types and values, including opaque values, and supplies inductive dependencies. A recursive walk with cycle detection can hash the dependency graph. The implementation must load the required private bodies, serialize declarations deterministically, and fail if a required body is unavailable. This is a syntactic artifact freeze; it can reject harmless refactoring and does not decide semantic equivalence. [Pinned implementation](/Users/francesco/.elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.30.0-rc2/src/lean/Lean/Util/FoldConsts.lean:65).
   371	- **Registry attributes:** feasible through checked attributes and a persistent environment extension. Check the elaborated certificate type, including its instance and bounds. A theorem with extra unproved premises must not appear as an unconditional certificate. Persistent extensions support imported registry data. [Lean environment API](https://lean-lang.org/doc/api/Lean/Environment.html).
   372	- **Kernel-checked refutations:** feasible for executable instance interfaces. `decide_cbv` does not require trust in compiled evaluation. A reflective checker needs a soundness theorem covering execution, regime and failed conclusion. Finite events alone do not make arbitrary hooks or function-valued environments decidable; use finite representations with equivalence proofs. [Lean tactic reference](https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Tactic-Proofs/Tactic-Reference/).
   373	- **Lassos:** correctly deferred. A repeating trace needs infinite-run semantics, fairness and a repetition or simulation theorem. Growing clocks and block stores usually require an abstract cycle. Parameterized finite counterexamples already suffice to refute every finite delay. [Existing Sanity theorem](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainWitnesses/Sanity.lean:295).
   374	
   375	A lasting implementation also needs an explicit extensible representation for `FacetBundle`, `FacetNeeds` and `ParamBinding`. Extending a frozen Lean structure with another field changes its declaration. Typed maps, separate facet records or another extension mechanism should be selected in Phase 0. The registry should also preserve proof status, assumptions, applicable output names and module versions; a paper result must not appear as a Lean certificate.
   376	
   377	For internal consistency, I found no stale operative `E7`, `LeftAlone` or `FGDomain` reference in v5. `Static` and `TargetPreserving` are no longer the actual v5 conditions. The material stale references are the pending r147/blueprint status and the unspecified I1–I3 shorthand. The current reports distinguish paper proofs, conditional implications and open Lean integration; the framework should retain those distinctions. [r147 report](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/reports/r147-fgsa-conditional.md:3), [blueprint status](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/fgsa-healing-blueprint.md:41).
   378	
   379	**REVISE.** Keep the layer split, shared facets, finite refutations and versioned definitions. Before adoption, repair E4, replace the FG conditions with exact causal statements, restrict height-relative retention to its supported scope, and close the timed composition interfaces. The Phase 0 prototype should demonstrate these boundaries before the framework is frozen.
