    93	**B06. Joint recovery has missing interface obligations.** Safe, advancing FG targets do not imply recovery of every exposed AP output. An AP can retain the required target behavior while a separate output chooses conflicting descendants of F after an asynchronous prefix. `ap.floored` still holds. `ap.cleanCompatible` says nothing about this recovery execution. Add conditional recovery claims for the ordinary outputs, including their relationship to targets and the handoff state.
