   127	**M06. Mechanical comparison needs a smaller, checked interface.** Arbitrary `Prop` relations are not computable orders. The schema also omits reflexivity and transitivity laws. Multidimensional tradeoffs can have several incomparable best certificates, so the registry needs a Pareto set, not one “strongest” constant tuple. Attributes must be checked against the actual certificate type and its facets. `Refutation` needs valid parameters before the registry reports it as a valid cell.
