   163	## 5. Invariants used by the composition (V03)
   164	
   165	Three separate invariants, each over execution prefixes:
   166	- clean history (GST = 0 regimes);
   167	- post-reset source history: from the reset boundary, each source body
   168	  from its first transfer HEAD q_s (not all pre-reset sources: old
   169	  justification disclosure is a counterexample, fgsa-fast.md);
   170	- armed-prefix Outage history: B only, not every later body (two
   171	  partition branches can both extend B).
   172	
   173	`Harmless` is stated as compatibility with the body being protected, not
   174	as provenance of one row of a new quorum.

