   179	Literal F constancy creates a separate bound issue. There is at most one branch-excluding top-J event at a fixed frontier, but there can be many lower F advances. Counting each as a new repair attempt gives an initial-frontier-dependent bound. The uniform bound requires a proof that exact service continues through harmless lower F advances. The blueprint marks that stronger interface SKETCH. v5 must select one form and its corresponding bound. [r147 count](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/fgsa-conditional.md:597), [bound consequence](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/fgsa-healing-blueprint.md:887).
