   181	**V07 — Arbitrary-horizon inhabitation is useful but does not prove meaningful coverage.** A witness can deliver heartbeats forever while having no eligible proposal, no non-genesis armed output, or no nonempty FG source. A protocol can also have long benign runs while a particular accepted input makes future synchrony impossible. Existential witnesses for each horizon do not prove continuation from that input. Witness obligations should be claim-specific and exercise the trigger and deadline; scheduler feasibility needs its own stated scope. [Witness requirement](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:359).
