   188	deliver it before the source's d_s test and remove that seat from p.
   189	Thus all p seats count as clean conflicts against every lease that
   190	conflicts with C. The release rule removes a lease at count `≥τ`,
   191	including `p=τ`. It also tests excluded leases. Expiry at equality occurs
   192	before release. Later equivocation cannot undo this completed snapshot.
   193	This is the release argument of SA's `fast_source_permanent_support`
   194	and `nextHeadState_conflict_stronger` [SA2, SA3].
