   138	Let r_G be the first action round with `a_(r_G) ≥ GST`. The DC cut is the
   139	inclusive event prefix at `u_0 = a_(r_G+2)`. Then `GST+2P ≤ u_0 < GST+3P`.
   140	Let M be the honest archival frontier at u_0. As in DC,
   141	
   142	```text
   143	H = the first multiple of K strictly above M+D+2;
   144	M+D+3 ≤ H ≤ M+D+K+2;  H+3 ≤ M+D+K+5.
   145	```
   146	
   147	### 1.3 Duty frames and "kept"
   148	
   149	A duty d is an honest HEAD (R1 view), proposal (full view), FG action
   150	(full view), or finality-head read (full view) at time t_d. For its view
   151	V_d the frame is, as in [fgsa-fast §2.1](fgsa-fast.md):
   152	
   153	```text
   154	F_d = accepted F;   H_d = max({1} ∪ {σ[W].h : W∈V_d});
   155	(j_d,J_d) = greatest (σ[W].h_j, σ[W].J) in V_d with F_d ⪯ σ[W].J;
   156	Z_d = J_d if H_d = j_d+1, else F_d;
   157	D_d = {B∈V_d : Z_d⪯B and ∃W∈V_d, B⪯W, σ[W].h ≥ H_d−1}.
   158	```
   159	
   160	Since `F_d⪯Z_d` always, the F test in D_d follows from the Z test.
   161	D_d is closed under ancestors down to Z_d.
   162	
   163	**Definition (kept).** A block B∈V_d is *kept* at d, written Kept_d(B),
   164	iff `B⪯Z_d` or `B∈D_d`. If B⪯Z_d, every walk result of d contains B,
   165	because the walk starts at Z_d or at a deeper lease in D_d. If B∈D_d, the
   166	walk can reach B, subject only to base scores and lease starts. A block
   167	that is not kept is *lost* at d.
   168	
   169	**Definition (effective filter).** For a duty d put
   170	`Ẑ_d = J_d` if `H_d = j_d+1` (J-mode), and `Ẑ_d = ◇` otherwise (F-mode).
   171	The effective filter is `Φ_d = (H_d, Ẑ_d)`. In F-mode, F_d is not part of
   172	Φ_d. Section 4 shows that this omission is harmless.
