   174	## 2. The hypotheses (a)
   175	
   176	### 2.1 Two forms of "no FG interference"
   177	
   178	**(N1) Static effective filter.** For times u≤v, a frontier m≥1, and
   179	`Ẑ ∈ {◇} ∪ Blocks`, (N1)(u,v;m,Ẑ) holds iff every honest duty d with
   180	t_d∈[u,v] satisfies: the honest frontier at t_d exceeds m, or
   181	`Φ_d = (m,Ẑ)`.
   182	
   183	(N1) permits these changes: arbitrary view growth, lease paths that enter
   184	or leave a HEAD view, F advances in F-mode (they are below the band, §4.1),
   185	lower J changes, and a finalization of J_(m−1) in J-mode. It forbids a
   186	change of the band threshold at a frontier that has not risen, and a
   187	change between the two modes.
   188	
   189	**(N2) Protected blocks are kept.** Let 𝒫 be a set of blocks, each with a
   190	start time q(B). (N2)(𝒫;t) holds iff every B∈𝒫 is kept at every honest
   191	duty d (HEAD, proposal, FG action, or finality head) with
   192	`q(B) ≤ t_d ≤ t`.
   193	
   194	(S) as used here needs only the HEAD and proposal clauses. The action and
   195	finality-head clauses are included so that (N2) contains r147's N2, which
   196	names every honest choice duty. Lemma K (§7.3) proves keep for every kind
   197	of honest view, so the extra clauses cost nothing.
   198	
   199	### 2.2 (S): conditional source safety
   200	
   201	A *fast body* at label s is a block B with `B∈FastWrite_i[s]` at some
   202	honest reader i. A *slow body* at label s is a block that receives a slow
   203	write at s at some honest reader, with a slow window `[s−k+1, s]`. A label
   204	s is *synchronous* iff `t_s ≥ GST` and E-env holds from t_s.
   205	
   206	**(S)** Let B be a fast body at a synchronous label s. Assume that all
   207	labels ≥ s are synchronous. Let t ≥ q_s. If (N2)({B};t) holds with
   208	q(B)=q_s, then:
   209	
   210	- (S1) every honest HEAD at a time in `[q_s, t]` contains B;
   211	- (S2) every honest proposal at a slot u with `u ≥ s+2` and `t_u ≤ t`
   212	  extends B;
   213	- (S3) every honest S at a time in `[d_(s+1), t]` contains B.
   214	
   215	(S1) and (S3) are the only clauses that Theorem N and H-FG use. (S2) is
   216	used only in Theorem H.
   217	
   218	**(S_slow)** The same statement for a slow body at label s, when its whole
   219	window `[s−k+1, s]` is synchronous.
   220	
   221	(S) is the blueprint's step 1 in the weakest form that the composition
   222	uses. It asks for *no* property of the filter except that B itself is kept.
   223	It asks for no FG participation and no static frame. It must hold for
   224	fast bodies at **every** label, not only at FG action labels: §7.7 needs it
   225	for all base leases. The proof obligation is the SA theorem
   226	[fast_source_permanent_support][sa-support] with the domain premise: a
   227	kept B either lies below the root, or lies in D_d with the path from the
   228	walk start. The release at τ, the transfer by strict score, the pending
   229	gate, and the S guard are then the unchanged SA steps. The composition
   230	does not use S at the vote time a_r.
   231	
   232	### 2.3 (L): conditional liveness
   233	
   234	**(L)** There is a constant λ>0 and a start time `u_L ≤ u_0` such that for
   235	every `u ≥ u_L`, every m≥1, and every Ẑ: if the honest frontier at u
   236	equals m and (N1)(u,u+λ;m,Ẑ) holds, then the honest frontier at u+λ
   237	exceeds m.
   238	
   239	(L) must be uniform over the base state at u: arbitrary S values, live
   240	and excluded leases, and saved raw results. It uses only E-env from GST.
   241	It is the blueprint's step 2. Its proof must produce the base repair in
   242	the domain, exact service, fresh fast writes, C_fg at every honest
   243	validator, rows (targets or timeouts, including the lock cases), a
   244	consuming carrier, and a rise. Section 9 instantiates λ.
   245	
   246	### 2.4 (X): exact service under a domain premise
   247	
   248	**(X)** Let P be an honest proposal at slot u after GST, with parent A.
   249	Assume:
   250	
   251	- (x1) every honest live lease target at v_u is a prefix of A;
   252	- (x2) at the proposal read and at every honest HEAD d at v_u,
   253	  `Z_d ⪯ A` and `h(A) ≥ H_d−1`.
   254	
   255	Then every honest HEAD at v_u names P, and every honest S contains P at
   256	`d_u = t_u+6Δ`.
   257	
   258	(x2) puts A, and the current-slot P, in D_d at each of these reads. (X)
   259	is then a pure base step. Its paper proof is the exact edge comparison of
   260	[fgsa-adjudicate §3.2](fgsa-adjudicate.md): there, (x1) is "every lease
   261	target precedes A", and (x2) is "every controlling checkpoint entry
   262	precedes A" and "h(A) ≥ H_read−1". The same proof covers the pending
   263	label-(u−1) gate. It follows the clean-inclusion order of
   264	[CleanInclusion][sa-inclusion]. The composition uses (X) only for full
   265	healing (§7.7). It is not part of (S) or (L) as the blueprint states
   266	them. Section 8 therefore lists it as an extra premise.
   267	
   268	### 2.5 Why these forms are weak enough, and not weaker
   269	
   270	(N2) cannot be dropped from (S). In the exact trace CE-1 of
   271	[fgsa-fast-opus §5.2](fgsa-fast-opus.md), the post-GST fast body Y9 is
   272	lost at the HEAD at 45 because the disclosed root X excludes it. The
   273	fast count and all SA release steps hold there. Thus some form of the
   274	domain premise is necessary, and "B is kept" is the smallest one.
   275	
   276	(N1) is weaker than "root, F, and band fixed", in two ways. It permits
   277	F advances in F-mode, and it permits all view growth. Section 4.1 proves
   278	that these changes do not change any band output. If (L) is proved only
   279	with literal F constancy, §9.4 gives the weaker, M-dependent bound.
   280	
   281	(L) cannot use (N2) as its premise. Before the reset there can be no
   282	protected block at all. Liveness then needs an interval in which the
   283	filter does not move.
