   319	
   320	**B1 — PROVED.** Let C_i and C_j be genuine results at label s at readers
   321	i and j, and suppose they conflict. Let E_i and E_j be their surviving
   322	early supporters. They are disjoint: a seat with early votes on both sides
   323	is an equivocator at both late tests, since each early vote reaches the
   324	other reader before d_s. Early receipt at one reader implies receipt in
   325	the other reader's late pool. Thus `E_i ∪ E_j ⊆ D_i ∩ D_j`. From
   326	`2|E_i|>|D_i| ≥ |E_i|+|E_j|` we get `|E_i|>|E_j|`, and symmetrically
   327	`|E_j|>|E_i|`. This is a contradiction.
   328	
   329	**B2 — PROVED.** A gate writes leases only on prefixes of a result X that
   330	is compatible with every live lease. For a live lease K, either K⪯X or
   331	X⪯K. In both cases every prefix of X is comparable with K. Release and
   332	expiry only remove leases. Induction over gates gives the claim.
   333	
   334	**Crossing lemma (F11) — PROVED.** Let V be a duty view with maximum
   335	`H_V = m'`, and W∈V a block of height m'. Let Q be the first block of
   336	height m' on the path to W. Then Q∈V, its parent has height m'−1 and
   337	entry T, and Q folds a quorum for (m'−1, T). By F1 one row is honest. Its
   338	source A has `T⪯A` and `h(A) = m'−1`. Let B∈V be compatible with A. If
   339	`h(B) ≥ m'−1`, B is its own band witness. Otherwise `h(B) < m'−1 = h(T)`,
   340	so B≺A, and B and T are both prefixes of A. Since `h(T) > h(B)`, `B≺T⪯Q`,
   341	and Q is a band witness above B in V itself. This is L4 of
   342	[fgsa-fast-opus §3.1](fgsa-fast-opus.md), with the view's own maximum.
   343	
   344	**Prefix lemma (F12) — PROVED.** If `X⪯Y` and Y is compatible with B, then
   345	X is comparable with B. Proof: if B⪯Y, then X and B are prefixes of Y; if
   346	Y≺B, then X⪯Y≺B.

