   558	### 7.3 One-duty keep lemma — PROVED
   559	
   560	**Lemma K.** Let d be an honest duty of any kind (HEAD, proposal, FG
   561	action, or finality head) with `t_d ≥ q_(s*)`, and let B∈𝒫 with
   562	`q(B) ≤ t_d`. Assume:
   563	
   564	- (K1) every honest row emitted before t_d at a height ≥ x+1 has a source
   565	  compatible with B and with C*;
   566	- (K2) NJ arm: no honest target row at x is emitted before t_d;
   567	  finalized arm: nothing (F3 and F4 supply the arm facts);
   568	- (K3) B is compatible with C*.
   569	
   570	Then Kept_d(B).
   571	
   572	Proof. B∈V_d and C*∈V_d by §7.1, so `H_d ≥ x+1`.
   573	
   574	*Root.* First show that Z_d is comparable with B.
   575	
   576	1. Z_d = J_d with `j_d = H_d−1 ≥ x`. If `j_d = x`, the NJ arm is excluded:
   577	   a justification at x needs an honest target row at x (F1), and K2 has
   578	   none. In the finalized arm, J_d = F* (F3). F* ⪯ C* by F4, since
   579	   `h(C*) = x+1 > x`. By K3 and F12, F* is comparable with B. If
   580	   `j_d ≥ x+1`, J_d has an honest target row at height j_d with a source
   581	   C_J, and `J_d ⪯ C_J`. By K1 and F12, J_d is comparable with B.
   582	2. Z_d = F_d. If `h(F_d) ≤ x`, then F_d ⪯ C* by F4, and F12 with K3 gives
   583	   comparability. If `h(F_d) ≥ x+1`, F_d is a justified entry at that
   584	   height. Its honest target row has a source C_F with `F_d ⪯ C_F`; K1 and
   585	   F12 give comparability.
   586	
   587	If B⪯Z_d, B is kept. Otherwise `Z_d ≺ B`, so `F_d ⪯ B`, and it remains to
   588	find a band witness in V_d.
   589	
   590	*Band.* Put `m′ = H_d ≥ x+1`. If `h(B) ≥ m′−1`, B is its own witness.
   591	Otherwise `h(B) ≤ m′−2`. If `m′−1 ≥ x+1`, the crossing row of F11 is at
   592	height `m′−1 ≥ x+1`, and K1 makes its source compatible with B; F11 gives
   593	a witness. If `m′−1 ≤ x`, then `m′ = x+1` and `h(B) ≤ x−1 < h(C*)`. By K3,
   594	B≺C*, and C* is a witness of height x+1 ≥ m′−1. ∎
