   603	### 7.4 No FG interference for ever — PROVED from (S), (S_slow)
   604	
   605	**Theorem N.** For every t, IH(t) holds. In particular (N2)(𝒫;t) holds
   606	for every t.
   607	
   608	Proof. A *failing event* is an honest duty that loses a block B∈𝒫 with
   609	q(B) ≤ its time, or, in the NJ arm, an honest target row at x. IH(t)
   610	fails exactly when a failing event occurs before t. Duty and action
   611	times lie on a discrete grid. Suppose that a failing event exists, and
   612	let t_d be the time of the earliest one. Then IH(t_d) holds.
   613	
   614	*Clause (i) fails at t_d.* Some honest duty d at t_d loses some B∈𝒫
   615	with `q(B) ≤ t_d`. By §6, every honest row at a height ≥ x+1 has its
   616	source in 𝒫. By Lemma C, K1 holds for B, and K3
   617	holds since C*∈𝒫. K2 is IH(t_d)(ii). Lemma K gives Kept_d(B). This is a
   618	contradiction.
   619	
   620	*Clause (ii) fails at t_d.* An honest validator emits a target row at x at
   621	action a_r = t_d. By F7, a_r is after the DC prefix. Since a_(r*) is in
   622	that prefix, r > r*. Its source
   623	C′ is in 𝒫 at height x. By Lemma C, C′ is compatible with C*; since
   624	`h(C′) = x < h(C*)`, C′ ≺ C*. Thus C′ lies on C*'s x-plateau. That plateau
   625	is in an honest store before `first`, so its nj bit is true (F6), and its
   626	entry is the same for C′ (F5). The signer has no target record at x: the
   627	prefix has none (F7), and after the prefix a record comes only from an
   628	earlier honest target row at x, which IH(t_d)(ii) excludes. The signer has
   629	no lock at x: a lock needs a justified entry at x, hence an earlier honest
   630	target row at x (F1). DC's `height_pair` then returns a timeout at x.
   631	This is a contradiction. ∎
   632	
   633	The finalized arm needs only clause (i). The NJ facts of F7 are used only
   634	for rows in the DC prefix. Clause (ii) extends them to all later rows by
   635	source compatibility. It does not claim that every later chain state at H
   636	is NJ.
