   716	2. *(x2) for honest proposals.* Let P be an honest proposal at a slot
   717	   u ≥ s*+2, with parent A, and let d be its proposal read or an honest
   718	   HEAD at v_u. By (S2), P extends every B∈𝒫 with label ≤ u−2. The slot
   719	   of such a B is at most its label, and P's slot is u, so B ⪯ A. In
   720	   particular C* ⪯ A. Every honest row that V_d can contain was emitted at an
   721	   action d_s < t_u+Δ, so its label is ≤ u−2. Hence every such row at a
   722	   height ≥ x+1 has a source that is a prefix of A. Root: repeat the root
   723	   part of Lemma K with "prefix of A" in place of "comparable with B".
   724	   J_d and F_d above x are prefixes of their honest sources, hence of A;
   725	   J at x is absent (NJ arm, N-b) or F* ⪯ C* (finalized arm); an F at
   726	   height ≤ x precedes C* (F4). So `Z_d ⪯ A`. Band: if the maximizing
   727	   crossing row of V_d is at height ≥ x+1, its entry T is a prefix of its
   728	   source, hence of A, so `h(A) ≥ h(T) = H_d−1`. Otherwise `H_d = x+1`
   729	   and `h(A) ≥ h(C*) = x+1`. Rows at heights ≤ x emitted before r* need
   730	   not precede A; they enter only through these two cases.
   731	3. *Repair.* By E-env an honest proposal P exists at a slot u ≥ β_b with
   732	   `t_u ≤ t_(β_b)+G`. At v_u every live lease is in 𝒫 (item 1) and has
   733	   label ≤ u−2, since a label-(u−1) lease is written at t_u+2Δ. By (S2)
   734	   it is a prefix of A, which is (x1). Item 2 gives (x2). By (X), every
   735	   honest S contains P at `d_u ≤ t_(s*)+2L−2Δ+G+6Δ = t_heal`.
   736	4. *Clean continuation.* From P on, every honest HEAD names the current
   737	   honest proposal (items 2–3 for each later honest proposal). Each gate
   738	   then has h clean supporters of one block, `2h > h+a` and `h ≥ τ`, so
   739	   every S write is a fast write and its block is in 𝒫. By Theorem N these
   740	   blocks are kept for ever. The S guard keeps S when the result is a
   741	   prefix. A result that conflicts with S is impossible, since both are
   742	   in 𝒫 and Lemma C makes them compatible. Thus (A) and (B) hold. (C) is
   743	   (X) at each later honest proposal.
   744	5. *Accessor.* Let F be held by an honest validator at a time ≥ t_heal.
   745	   If `h(F) ≤ x`, then F ⪯ C* ⪯ S by F4. Otherwise F is justified at a
   746	   height ≥ x+1, and its target QC has an honest row at some round r_J
   747	   with source C_J ∈ 𝒫 and `F ⪯ C_J`. An honest finality pair for F needs
   748	   a head that already carries this QC, so it is emitted at an action
   749	   `≥ a_(r_J)+P`, and F is accepted later. Since `P ≥ 4Δ`, every honest S
   750	   contains C_J, hence F, from `a_(r_J)+4Δ` on. So `F ⪯ S`. ∎
   751	
   752	The healthy continuation in item 4 is the induction of
   753	[fgsa-adjudicate §3.2](fgsa-adjudicate.md) with its domain premises
   754	supplied by Theorem N instead of a healthy prefix.
