   756	### 7.8 What is not claimed: full healing already at q_(s*)
   757	
   758	**H12 — OPEN.** Theorem H pays the SA two-lease repair after s*. The
   759	composition does not show that it is necessary. The mechanism that it
   760	guards against is this, with `n=7, a=2, h=5, τ=4`. Let two honest
   761	validators hold a live lease on Y ⪰ C* whose source label is before s*.
   762	The release at q_(s*) does not remove it, because Y is compatible with
   763	C*. Let X ⪰ C* be a sibling of Y.
   764	
   765	1. At a label s ≥ s*, three honest HEADs name X. The two Y holders start
   766	   their walks at Y and name Y. The faulty seats are silent. Every reader
   767	   has `p(X)=3, |D|=5`, and `6>5`, so X is genuine everywhere. Since
   768	   `3<τ`, no fast lease is written. The three readers without the Y
   769	   lease write S:=X. The Y holders fail the guard and keep S.
   770	2. At label s+1 the same five honest HEADs repeat, and the two faulty
   771	   seats name Y in time for every early cutoff. Every reader has
   772	   `p(Y)=4, |D|=7`, `8>7`, and `4≥τ`. No live lease conflicts with Y at
   773	   the X readers, so they write S:=Y. X leaves their S.
   774	
   775	X is not in 𝒫 (no fast write, no slow window). Y becomes a fast body at
   776	label s+1, so it is in 𝒫 from then on. No FG object takes part, and every
   777	protected block stays kept. The label counts are exact. A complete
   778	reachable prefix that leaves such a Y lease at s* is not written here, so
   779	this is a SKETCH mechanism, not a refutation. It shows that "FG-healed"
   780	and "healed" are different statements. With `n=4`, `p > |D|/2 ≥ 3/2`
   781	gives `p ≥ 2 = τ`, so every S write is fast and this mechanism does not
   782	occur.
