  1026	### 9.4 Composition with r147's (L) as proved — PROVED*, M-dependent
  1027	
  1028	r147's N1 fixes F, Z, and H_d. Every F advance then interrupts the
  1029	static interval, and r147 §6 charges a full `W = 3Δ+B_static` after
  1030	each counted event. Put `λ = λ_147` and use θ=4Δ ≥ 3Δ. At frontier m
  1031	the number of interruptions is at most `1 + n_F(m)`, where n_F(m) counts
  1032	new finalized heights that first appear at frontier m. The case split
  1033	of Theorem HP then gives at most `(2+n_F(m))(λ+θ)` per level. The
  1034	accepted F only increases, and it stays ≤ H+1 before the frontier
  1035	reaches H+3. Thus `Σ_m n_F(m) ≤ H+2−f_0`, with f_0 the least honest h_F
  1036	at u_0, and
  1037	
  1038	```text
  1039	T_arr  ≤ u_0 + [2(D+K+5) + (H+2−f_0)](λ+θ)
  1040	       ≤ u_0 + [3(D+K+5) + M](λ+θ);
  1041	t_heal < GST + 3P + [3(D+K+5) + M](λ+θ) + 2L + G − 2Δ.
  1042	```
  1043	
  1044	This bound depends on the initial frontier M, which the pre-GST adversary
  1045	controls. r147's per-level count `N ≤ m−1−f0+ε_J` is the same bound
  1046	before summation. The trunk lemma of §4.1 removes the M term, provided
  1047	that (L) holds under the effective filter (H16, §10).
