   525	## 6. Fixed-height filter changes — PROVED
   526	
   527	Fix a post-GST interval on which the honest archival frontier is m.
   528	It is the maximum over honest accepted histories, not one frozen HEAD.
   529	Let j0 and f0 be the greatest justified and finalized heights in that
   530	accepted history at the interval start. Include genesis at height 0.
   531	They satisfy `0≤f0≤j0≤m−1`. All counts below are integer counts of
   532	distinct control evidence, not counts of receivers of the same object.
   533	
   534	**Certificate facts.** Two different justified entries at one positive
   535	height need two target quorums. Their intersection has at least
   536	`2q_F−n>a` identities, including an honest double target. DC's record
   537	rule excludes it [DC4]. A finalized checkpoint at height f precedes
   538	every chain block of height greater than f: otherwise its finality
   539	quorum and a crossing quorum at f yield an honest E1 conflict [DC5].
   540	These arguments include private certificates and old signatures. They
   541	do not date a target by the receipt time of its carrier.
   542	
   543	**Late maximum witnesses.** A carrier attaining m reaches every honest
   544	full view strictly before u+Δ. It remains admissible after any F
   545	advance under this cap: its height m is greater than the finalized
   546	height. A HEAD at time x uses a freeze at x−2Δ. Thus every HEAD from
   547	u+3Δ has an m witness in its own view. The R1 additions cannot raise
   548	the view above the fixed honest archival cap. From that time `H_d=m`
   549	at every duty. The same argument gives a 3Δ settling allowance after
   550	any newly accepted controlling event. A P allowance also suffices.
   551	
   552	The control carriers must be admitted as well as delivered. In a quiet
   553	interval let F* be the greatest accepted finalization. Each local F
   554	precedes F*. A carrier for F* extends the local F. A higher selected J
   555	extends F* by [DC5]; an equal-height J equals F* by [DC4]. Thus the
   556	`F*⪯J` acceptance test holds. For viability, either the local maximum
   557	is at most h(F*)+1 and the finality carrier supplies the witness, or a
   558	higher maximizing block extends F* by [DC5]. The acceptance test succeeds
   559	when the complete carrier is processed. It need not replay a refused
   560	update. Likewise, a top-J carrier of height m extends every local F
   561	under the cap. These facts give common F and the top root after relay;
   562	the freeze margin gives those same controls at R1 HEADs. An equal-height
   563	carrier cannot change their names, by uniqueness.
   564	
   565	A later witness of height at most m does not raise this band. With
   566	F and Z fixed, it only adds viable paths. It is not a new exclusion.
   567	There can be arbitrarily many such blocks; their count is not bounded
   568	by the number of control changes. Before settling, full and frozen
   569	reads can alternate. No monotone potential on the sequence of actual
   570	duty tuples is claimed. This is the R1 distinction in
   571	[fg-frame-recovery §2.3](fg-frame-recovery.md) and the settling argument
   572	in [fg-settling §2](fg-settling.md), with the PC arms removed.
   573	
   574	**Top J and lower J.** After H_d=m settles, only J at m−1 can activate
   575	the J root. At positive height it has one possible name. If it was
   576	not yet known, its first disclosure can change the selected branch
   577	once. An additional carrier for that same J is not another event.
   578	A lower J changes neither Z nor the band when the gate is off; when
   579	the top gate is on, it cannot replace the top J. It can add blocks to
   580	the view, which the exact service proof already permits.
   581	
   582	**F advances.** A proper F advance has a larger finalized height:
   583	finalized checkpoints at an equal height are the same justified entry.
   584	Under this cap its height is at most m−1. Thus there are at most
   585	`m−1−f0` new aggregate F levels. Local readers can catch up to old
   586	levels as well. Their initial catch-up takes the same relay margin;
   587	it is not a new adversarial certificate.
   588	
   589	If `f_new≤m−2`, every band witness W extends F_new by [DC5]. A
   590	previous retained prefix B witnessed by W either precedes F_new, or
   591	remains witnessed above it. Such a finalization cannot exclude a band
   592	branch. If `f_new=m−1`, it supplies the unique top J and is charged
   593	to that same possible branch exclusion. Once Z=J at m−1, every later
   594	F under the cap precedes J or equals it; the predicate `F⪯B` is then
   595	redundant above Z.
   596	
   597	This proves at most one **branch-excluding** event. For N1's literal
   598	F-constancy premise, this file nevertheless counts every aggregate F
   599	advance and allows settling and repair after it. It does not need a
   600	stronger exact-service theorem through changing finality bases.
   601	
   602	Define `ε_J=1` if `m≥2` and `j0<m−1`, and `ε_J=0` otherwise.
   603	
   604	```text
   605	┌──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┐
   606	│ Evidence or control change           │ Maximum new count at fixed m │
   607	├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
   608	│ Positive-height J at m−1             │ ε_J                          │
   609	│ Strict aggregate F advances          │ m−1−f0                       │
   610	│ Strict aggregate lower-J advances    │ max(0,m−2−j0)                │
   611	│ Lower-J changes of the filter rule   │ 0                            │
   612	│ Late ≤m witnesses after band settles │ 0 exclusions                 │
   613	│ Initial band/old-cache catch-up      │ 1 settling allowance         │
   614	│ New F/top-J control events for N1    │ N ≤ m−1−f0+ε_J               │
   615	│ Branch-excluding events              │ at most ε_J                  │
   616	└──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┘
   617	```
   618	
   619	The event bound may count a combined F/top-J disclosure twice; it is
   620	a safe upper bound. At m=1 all new control counts are zero. If individual
   621	accepted-F updates are wanted, each of the h honest readers makes at
   622	most m−1 such positive-height updates over the whole capped prefix,
   623	so `h(m−1)` bounds their total. The public-evidence count above is the
   624	one used for recovery; it does not multiply a bullet by its recipients.
   625	
   626	After the last relevant F/top-J event and 3Δ of settling, all duties
   627	have the same F, band m, and root Z. This is N1. Lower J disclosures
   628	can continue without breaking N1. This proves the fixed-height filter
