   733	\subsection{Chain state and transition}
   734	
   735	Every block is evaluated from its parent's immutable post-state:
   736	\[
   737	 \sigma[B]=\Call{state\_transition}{\sigma[B.\parent],B}.
   738	\]
   739	\begin{definition}[Chain state]\label{def:chain-state}
   740	A chain state is
   741	\[
   742	 \sigma=(L,s,h,T_h,\nj,
   743	  \targetParticipation,\progressBit,\finalityBit,
   744	  J,h_j,F,h_F).
   745	\]
   746	$\sigma.L$ is the latest block, $\sigma.s=\sigma.L.\slot$, $\sigma.h$ is the
   747	current height, and $\sigma.T_h$ is the block that brought the transition
   748	into height~$\sigma.h$.  The Boolean $\sigma.\nj$ is computed when the chain
   749	enters~$\sigma.h$ and remains fixed until the height
   750	changes.
   751	
   752	The arrays $\sigma.\targetParticipation$, $\sigma.\progressBit$, and
   753	$\sigma.\finalityBit$ contain
   754	one Boolean value per validator.  Their quorum sets are derived when used:
   755	\[
   756	 \begin{aligned}
   757	  \Qtarget(\sigma)&=\{i:\sigma.\targetParticipation[i]\},&
   758	  \Qprog(\sigma)&=\{i:\sigma.\progressBit[i]\},\\
   759	  \Qfin(\sigma)&=\{i:\sigma.\finalityBit[i]\}.&&
   760	 \end{aligned}
   761	\]
   762	The pair $(\sigma.J,\sigma.h_j)$ is the latest justification on the chain,
   763	and $(\sigma.F,\sigma.h_F)$ is its latest finalization.  Initially
   764	\[
   765	 \sigma.L=\sigma.T_h=\sigma.J=\sigma.F=\genesis,\quad
   766	 \sigma.s=0,\quad \sigma.h=1,\quad \sigma.h_j=\sigma.h_F=0,
   767	 \quad\sigma.\nj=\mathsf{false},
   768	\]
   769	and every array entry is false.
   770	\end{definition}
   771	
   772	Fix constants $K\geq4$, $D\geq2$ and a timeout delay $\delta_{\mathrm{t}}\geq0$ in slots; $K$ is meant large, $D$ minimal, and \S\ref{sec:healing} sets $\delta_{\mathrm{t}}=2R$, two rounds.  A height pair counts only when it names the chain's own entry at the current height: a target vote then records target participation and progress, a timeout records progress alone, and a pair naming another entry records nothing, while its finality pair is folded regardless.  Timeouts are recorded in $\progressBit$ as soon as they are folded, but a progress quorum that needs them is consumed only by a block whose slot is at least $\sigma.T_h.\slot+\delta_{\mathrm{t}}$, where $\sigma.T_h$ is the block that entered the height; an exact target quorum is consumed immediately: attestations are synchronous at the scale of rounds, so a timeout may not be used to leave a height before the target votes cast at that height have had time to arrive.  Without the delay, faulty timeouts released right after an honest block that folded a partial honest target batch can cross the height without justifying it.
   773	
   774	The steady pipeline enters heights at debt $\sigma.h-\sigma.h_F=2$, so $D\geq2$;
   775	$K\geq3$ avoids a skip cadence that regenerates itself at $K=2$; $K\geq4$ is required because finality liveness needs a proposer gap $g\geq2$ with $g+2\leq K$, so $K=3$ would admit no run with the liveness premises.
   776	On entry into a new height~$\sigma.h$, after
   777	the same transition has applied any finalization, set
   778	\[
   779	 \sigma.\nj\gets(K\mid\sigma.h)\wedge(\sigma.h-\sigma.h_F>D).
   780	\]
