    75	T_r = rP;  P = 4RΔ;     a_r = T_r+6Δ = d_(rR);  R ≥ 3;
    76	δ_t = 2R slots;          D ≥ 2;  g ≥ 3;  K ≥ g+2;
    77	w_F ≥ 1 rounds for the attestation inclusion window.
    78	
    79	a < h ≤ n−a  ⇒  a < τ, q_F > a, 2h > h+a.
    80	a ≤ f       ⇒  h=n−a ≥ q_F, h>2a, h≥τ, 2q_F−n>a.
    81	```
    82	
    83	`q_s` denotes a time; `q_F` denotes a count. No count combines seats from
    84	different base labels. No SG participation window, grade-forming majority,
    85	or condition `R η_SG ≥ 4` remains. The inclusion window `w_F` serves only
    86	attestation transport. It is not a grade window or a source qualification.
    87	
    88	Recovery assumes full participation after GST, `a≤f`, strict Δ delivery
    89	and return relay, and an awake honest base proposer strictly after each
    90	trigger and within G. In addition, retain DC's multi-proposer recurrence:
    91	an honest opening and its next two slot proposers within g rounds. First
    92	finality uses DC's stronger recurrence: three consecutive honest openings,
    93	with the last opening's next two slot proposers honest. In continuous time
    94	this requires `g≥3`, hence `K≥5`. Every proof window must fit in the horizon.
    95	
    96	## 2. Exact base/FG coupling
    97	
    98	### 2.1 The domain has priority for choice
    99	
   100	Run the SA proposal and HEAD walks **inside the FG domain**. This is the
   101	role of the filtered tree in DC §7. Keeping a mandatory lease outside that
   102	domain while permitting height sources only inside it recreates the two
   103	different branch choices in entry-capture §6. Removing PC does not make
   104	two incompatible mandatory roots compatible.
   105	
   106	Keep R1's explicit duty view. At a HEAD in slot s, its block view contains:
   107	
   108	1. FG-admitted blocks before the previous-slot freeze `t_s−Δ`;
   109	2. ancestors of admitted current-slot proposals;
   110	3. admitted paths of the declared support votes;
   111	4. admitted paths of live SA lease targets;
   112	5. the evidence basis for the current accepted F.
   113	
   114	Take ancestor closure. A path adds no vote or support key. The raw/support
   115	vote merge is the SA merge: frozen previous-label votes plus the original
   116	declared subsets in current proposals. A raw-only declaration does not
   117	become declared support when its path later arrives. Full proposal and FG
   118	reads use the full processed admitted view.
   119	
   120	For the view V of one duty, calculate all control values together:
   121	
   122	```text
   123	F_d = current accepted F;
   124	H_d = max({1} ∪ {σ[W].h : W∈V});
   125	(j_d,J_d) = greatest (σ[W].h_j, root(σ[W].J)) in V with F_d ⪯ σ[W].J;
   126	Z_d = J_d if H_d=j_d+1, else F_d;
   127	
   128	D_d = {B∈V : F_d⪯B, Z_d⪯B,
   129	              and ∃W∈V, B⪯W and σ[W].h≥H_d−1}.
   130	```
   131	
   132	The full store also retains DC's monotone archival maximum. It supplies
   133	the causal frontier; it is not substituted for an unwitnessed HEAD maximum.
   134	R1 is an explicit change to DC's use of live control caches at that read.
   135	Its reason remains valid without PC: an arbitrary late witness must not
   136	raise the threshold in a frozen view that lacks that witness.
   137	
   138	Process finality live, in DC order. Retain its accepting carrier, the J
   139	carrier used at acceptance, and the descendant that witnessed F's viability.
   140	Include this basis in each later duty view. Do not reconstruct an older F
   141	from a receipt subset. At acceptance with full maximum M, the saved witness
   142	has height at least M−1. In a later view with maximum at most M it still
   143	witnesses F. A greater maximum has an admitted witness from after the F
   144	advance and therefore extends F. Thus F remains viable at every duty.
   145	
   146	Let M_d be the deepest live lease target in D_d, or Z_d if there is none.
   147	A lease on an ancestor of Z_d is already satisfied. A conflicting or
   148	nonviable lease remains stored but has no choice authority at this duty.
   149	The exact choice is:
   150	
   151	```text
   152	score(B) = number of equivocating seats in the raw view
   153	           + non-equivocating declared supporters above B;
   154	
   155	eligible(child) = σ[child.parent].h < H_d−1
   156	                 or 2*score(child) > number of raw participants
   157	                 or child.slot = currentSlot;
   158	
   159	HEAD = GHOST(M_d, D_d, score, eligible).
   160	```
   161	
   162	There is no F4 walk, PC start, grade start, or unfiltered fallback. The
   163	root can be returned if there is no eligible child. This is SA's mandatory
   164	lease start, restricted to DC's domain, with DC's below-band eligibility.
   165	It is not definitionally the standalone `sa` executable instance.
   166	
   167	### 2.2 SA gates stay unfiltered
   168	
   169	Retain the raw SA tree and signature archive separately from FG admission.
   170	Valid base evidence is processed for receipt, resolution, and equivocation
   171	even when its branch has no FG choice authority. FG block admission still
   172	requires descent from accepted F. Both trees refer to the same block bodies
   173	and immutable parent states; an off-parent carrier does not alter a parent's
   174	state.
   175	
   176	At q_s, expire deadlines at or before q_s. Count resolved non-equivocating
   177	label-s conflicts against each live lease and release it at count `≥τ`.
   178	Then run the next HEAD. Do not apply this snapshot to later writes.
   179	
   180	At d_s, use SA's early numerator and late denominator on the unfiltered
   181	base tree. Save the raw genuine result, including `none`, once. Remove
   182	equivocating seats from its numerator. If its result X is absent, or
   183	conflicts with any live lease, make no S or lease write. Otherwise:
   184	
   185	```text
   186	S := old S if X⪯old S, else X;
   187	for each non-genesis B⪯X:
   188	    fast := p_i(s,B) ≥ τ;
   189	    slow := all k saved results at s−k+1,...,s exist and contain B;
   190	    if fast or slow: E_i(B) := max(E_i(B), d_s+L).
   191	```
   192	
   193	The guard checks **all** live leases, including ones outside D_d. A domain
   194	change neither deletes a lease nor directly writes S. The slow test needs
   195	k actual consecutive results; missing labels cannot be skipped. An ancestor
   196	result cannot renew an unsupported child. There is no PC veto or capBroken
   197	mode. There is no second DC confirmation computation.
   198	
   199	This conservative gate rule permits recovery: an old conflicting lease
   200	can obstruct a write, but it cannot keep the HEAD outside D_d. New support
   201	can release it; the remaining unsupported writes have the two-lease bound
   202	within a retained effective domain (§9).
   203	
   204	## 3. One fresh source and the exact client
   205	
   206	### 3.1 Fresh means a successful fast write at this label
   207	
   208	Keep an immutable gate result and a local set `FastWrite_i[s]` at each
   209	completed gate. A block is in this set exactly when all of the following
   210	held at d_s:
   211	
   212	```text
   213	B ≠ genesis;
   214	C_i[s] exists and B⪯C_i[s];
   215	2*p_i(s,B) > |D_i[s]| and p_i(s,B) ≥ τ;
   216	the whole-result SA lease guard passed;
   217	the gate executed its lease write or renewal for B by the fast test.
   218	```
   219	
   220	The count is the surviving early support of **one** label after the late
   221	equivocation test. A raw signature quorum, a slow renewal, a received block,
   222	and the mere presence of a live E(B) do not satisfy this definition. If
   223	both admission tests pass, record the fast fact. A renewal counts even
   224	when a stored deadline comparison would leave the numerical value unchanged.
   225	
   226	At the FG action a_r, after the scheduled gate, put s=rR. This is the
   227	latest scheduled SA gate, including a gate that returned no result. Use:
   228	
   229	```text
   230	Candidates = {B∈D_action : B∈FastWrite_i[s] and E_i(B)>a_r};
   231	C_fg = deepest candidate, or none if Candidates is empty.
   232	```
   233	
   234	No older set may replace an empty `FastWrite_i[s]`. Sleeping does not make
   235	an old gate the latest gate. The candidates lie on the local raw result's
   236	ancestor path, so the deepest choice is unique. A deterministic root tie
   237	rule can be retained but is not needed on a valid local path.
   238	
   239	B need not have slot s. In particular, the source can be an old block with
   240	a fresh fast renewal. Its immutable entry `T=σ[B].T_h` can be older still.
   241	The height pair uses `(σ[B].h,T,σ[B].nj)`, not the source's slot and not
   242	the cache maximum. The source qualification applies before every client
   243	branch. A repeat still needs a current fresh source, but **the named entry
   244	does not need a new lease or a new slot**.
   245	
   246	This is a local source fact, not a new publicly verifiable certificate.
   247	Remote signatures cannot prove the absence of another signature at a
   248	private cutoff. Public validation authenticates the FG row and its named
   249	blocks, as in DC. Source soundness is an honest-duty theorem. The threshold
   250	`q_F>a` lets a certificate proof use an honest source when it needs one.
   335	
   336	These are two ledger tips, F and available. There is no strong accessor.
   337	No voting rule reads an output accessor. Pointwise `F⪯available` follows
   338	from its two cases, with no fault or synchrony premise. It does not imply
   339	`F⪯S` in an arbitrary damaged state.
   340	
   341	```text
   342	┌────────────────────────────────┬─────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┐
   343	│ Earlier rule                   │ Choice  │ Reason                                │
   344	├────────────────────────────────┼─────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
   345	│ R1: view-consistent band       │ KEPT    │ A duty needs its own height witness.  │
   346	│ R3: DC client branch order     │ KEPT    │ Locks and repeats remain necessary.   │
   347	│ R3: PC origin DAG / FreshOK    │ REMOVED │ No PC and no entry-slot test.         │
   348	│ R5(b): longer consumption age  │ REMOVED │ Restore DC's 2R; source qualifies     │
   349	│                                │         │ every timeout before signing.         │
   350	│ R6: timeout signing timer      │ REMOVED │ Same fresh-source rule for all hp.    │
   351	│ r106: exact current opening    │ REMOVED │ Fresh label, not fresh entry.         │
   352	│ r112: domain priority          │ KEPT    │ One choice domain; no SA fallback.    │
   353	│ r110: opening-only consumption │ REMOVED │ Old entries can receive targets.      │
   354	│ R4: PC/lease ancestor clamp    │ REMOVED │ Select actual fresh writes in D.      │
   355	│ SG grades and safe gossip      │ REMOVED │ SA replaces the whole available unit. │
   356	│ PC, acks, F4, capBroken        │ REMOVED │ These are not plain SA rules.         │
   357	└────────────────────────────────┴─────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┘
   358	```
   359	
   360	Removing a timer is a rule decision. The environment theorem that would
   361	show it is unnecessary is still subject to §10's history obligation.
   362	
   363	## 5. Base preservation for all a<h
   364	
   365	### 5.1 Two local domain lemmas — PROVED
   366	
   367	**A received crossing gives its own band witness.** Let B be a protected
   368	prefix present in a duty view. Suppose its maximum is m+1. On a maximizing
   369	carrier's path take the first block Q that entered m+1. Its exact-entry
   370	progress quorum has an honest signer because `q_F>a`. Let A be that
   371	signer's actual source, and T its height-m entry. If A is compatible with B,
   372	
   373	```text
   374	T⪯A; h(T)=h(A)=m; T⪯Q;
   375	T⪯B  ⇒ h(B)≥m;
   376	B≺T  ⇒ B⪯Q, with Q in this very duty view.
   377	```
   378	
   379	Thus B is viable if F_d⪯B. If B⪯F_d, the floor already contains B.
   380	The conclusion uses source compatibility, not only entry compatibility.
   381	An old T below a fork is compatible with both sides of that fork.
   382	
   383	**A fresh write respects every local live lease.** Every candidate comes
   384	from a successful whole-result gate. Its source is therefore compatible
   385	with every live lease at its action. During an armed first-loss induction,
   386	this supplies the preceding lemma for new signatures. Historical signatures
   387	need the healthy history; receipt after arming does not make them new.
   388	
   389	### 5.2 Clean history and exact service — SKETCH
   390	
   391	The intended simultaneous induction has four clauses:
   392	
   393	1. Every raw genuine result transfers to the next actual HEAD and all
   394	   later healthy HEADs, including results before the lease guard.
   395	2. Every emitted FG source is a prefix of one of those genuine results.
   396	   Hence all earlier honest source bodies are compatible with the current
   397	   protected genuine prefix.
   398	3. Every controlling height carrier retains that prefix by §5.1. Every
   399	   controlling J or F is compatible with it, since its target quorum has

