   329	For one fixed view V, advancing F to F′ removes only the trunk below
   330	F′. Every viable block is comparable with F′. Below F′ there is one
   331	viable child at each step, and the below-band clause makes it eligible.
   332	Above F′ the domain, scores, and eligibility are unchanged. Thus the
   333	walk has the same result. In J-mode the root is the fixed top J, and
   334	lower F changes are redundant. This proves H2 in the form needed here.
