   342	Every new lower F precedes A. Hence B either precedes the new root or
   343	remains on an admitted path to A. Its band witness persists. A fixed
   344	top J gives the same conclusion. The fast release and wholly new slow
   345	expiry arguments of §2 therefore apply. After transfer, each next
   346	honest batch provides a new witness of height at least `m−1` on B's
