   124	
   125	These results concern time truncation, not an arbitrary list prefix halfway through equal-time events. Such a list prefix can violate `tick_total`. [Schedule:38](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainStatements/Generic/Conditions.lean:38), [regimes:14](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainStatements/Generic/Regimes.lean:14), [StrongArmed:19](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainStatements/Strong/Regimes.lean:19).
   126	
   127	**M06. Mechanical comparison needs a smaller, checked interface.** Arbitrary `Prop` relations are not computable orders. The schema also omits reflexivity and transitivity laws. Multidimensional tradeoffs can have several incomparable best certificates, so the registry needs a Pareto set, not one “strongest” constant tuple. Attributes must be checked against the actual certificate type and its facets. `Refutation` needs valid parameters before the registry reports it as a valid cell.
   128	
   129	Further, `monoPrem` transports `holds`, not `RegimeInhabited`. Strengthening a premise can remove every witness. The mandatory fault is impossible for `faultCap = 0`, and for the current Fast regime at n = 4, which requires fewer than one faulty validator. Allow boundary-case witnesses and keep witness transport as a separate obligation. [Design:259](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:259), [design:343](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:343), [BelowQuarter:209](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainStatements/Generic/Conditions.lean:209).
   130	
   131	**M07. The proposed imports form a cycle.** L1 defines conditions using `anchorsOf` and runs of `AP ⊗ HavocFG`, but those definitions belong to L5. This directly conflicts with the L0–L3 import rule. Move the shared FG semantics and composition signatures to a lower definition layer. Leave implementation-specific proofs and derived theorems in the kits. This is an architectural issue, not a Lean limitation. [Import rule:79](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:79), [anchor ownership:442](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:442), [conditions:494](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:494).
   132	
   133	**M08. Refutation forms need separate semantics.** A checked finite run can refute a current bounded claim. The finite `Run` type does not yet define unbounded “eventually.” A lasso requires an infinite-run interpretation, fairness conditions, and a proof that its repeated part remains valid. Exact repetition is unlikely when clocks, blocks, and records grow; an abstract cycle needs a simulation theorem. Also, a lasso is not necessary to prove that no constant works: the existing Sanity theorem already uses a parameterized family of finite runs. [Design:372](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:372), [Run:114](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainModel/Generic/Run.lean:114), [all-delay refutation:295](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/AvailableChainWitnesses/Sanity.lean:295).
   134	
   135	**M09. The freeze boundary must itself be frozen.** Stopping dependency hashing at L0 is safe only if CI also verifies that each L0 version still names the same definitions. Otherwise an in-place engine edit escapes the catalog lock. Include declaration types and bodies, inductive definitions, opaque dependencies where relevant, and the pinned toolchain/dependency manifest. Separately identify the instance and facets used by each certificate. A semantic freeze is not a substitute for kernel checking. [Design:387](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:387).
   136	
   137	For the two minor findings:
   138	
   139	- **N01:** `ClaimSpec` has no `RegimeInhabited` field although `Cert` uses it. `FinalityHead` is absent from the facet table. The use of `ProtocolSpec n` needs reconciliation with the new per-label interface. `FGDomain` remains in the layer table. E7 and `LeftAlone` are clearly historical references, so their mere presence is not a defect. The r146 result now exists; r147’s requested output was not present in the inspected files. The “no design items open” statement is therefore premature. [Schema:259](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:259), [open items:664](/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain/docs/FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md:664), [r146 report:3](/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/reports/r146-fgsa-adjudicate.md:3).
